# Tests that differ from the reference, one a line: the test's name, then
# the reason. tests/rom/run.py reports each as KNOWN, never as ok; a known
# test that starts passing is reported too, so this list is kept true.
#
# alu (42), a difference the contract makes on purpose (README.md, Time):
# the test reads the multiplier or divider ($4214-$4217) while it works, a
# cycle or a few after its start; the multiplier and divider are done when
# read here. Every other read and every picture matches.
#
# replay (14), not yet explained: one read of the latched H counter ($213C) a dot off, or one
# pixel, after an access the replay started 2 clocks late: the work RAM's
# refresh before it ended 2 clocks later than the reference's. Why the
# reference's refresh starts there is not yet known (its own formula gives
# nativeshvc's clock); every other read and pixel matches.
